  "transcriber_notes": [
   "Rows: main part 74 as printed (臺北, 臺南, 高雄 blocks each with 合計 男女計, then 總計 男女計, 大正十三年, 同十二年, 同十一年 男女計); second part 6 (大正十年, 同九年 男女計). Spread pp.72-73 and pp.74-75 are one table (running head 外國渡歸航者……終 on p.75).",
   "Row labels are built from the printed hierarchy: 州廳, then 支那 / 英領 / 佛領 / 米領 / 蘭領 (nationality) where printed, place, then sex (男 女 計). Left page (pp.72, 74) holds 渡航者 農業 to 家事使用人; right page (pp.73, 75) holds 渡航者 無職業, 計 and all of 歸航者.",
   "The sex glyph of the single-row entries 海口 (臺北 支那) and 花蓮港 (table 57) is printed as a tiny 'ﾊ'-like mark; read as 男 because the column sums of 臺北 支那 計 男/女 (and, in table 57, 總計 男/女) reconcile only so.",
   "Row 同 十一年 男: 渡航者 計 '1,345' has a small figure under it that is not legible (only the first digit '1' can be made out): written '1,345 (1)[?]'. (The women's 8 and the 計 27 would imply 19; not used.)",
   "Small-type figures: a few cells carry a second, much smaller figure printed under the main figure and marked '(1)' at its left; footnote '(1)ハ朝鮮人ナリ' says these are 朝鮮人 (Koreans). Written here as '<main figure> (1)<small figure>', e.g. '140 (1)2'. The small figures are very small on the scan; each was read at crop size, and where two small digits were printed (e.g. 20, 27) both were read. Row sums of the small figures and male+female=total of the small figures were checked and reconcile wherever every small figure was read.",
   "Checks (python): in every row 渡航者 計 = sum of the occupation columns and 歸航者 計 = sum of its columns; 男+女 = 計 in every block (main figures and small figures); 支那 計, 合計 (臺北 / 臺南 / 高雄) and 總計 male/female/計 equal the sums of their component rows in all 22 columns - all reconcile. Second part: all row sums and 男+女=計 reconcile.",
   "Second part: the 渡航者 columns are printed on p.74 and the 計 / 歸航者 columns on p.75."
  ],
